1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,886
Hello everyone

2
00:00:07,886 --> 00:00:15,772
I am Prince Pundir, and today I am excited to present SafeWalk RaahSaathi, an autonomous, AI-grounded women's safety navigation platform

3
00:00:15,772 --> 00:00:23,658
Every day, millions of women commute home from universities and workplaces

4
00:00:23,658 --> 00:00:31,544
Mainstream navigation apps optimize purely for speed, often routing women through dark, unmonitored alleys just to save ninety seconds

5
00:00:31,544 --> 00:00:39,430
SafeWalk redefines navigation by prioritizing human safety over transit time, combining real road geometry, verified assistance havens, and explainable spatial intelligence

6
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:46,458
Let us see it in action

7
00:00:46,458 --> 00:00:53,487
Starting our journey in Dehradun at 10:00 PM, notice our dual routing: the red dashed line is the shortest path, cutting through high-risk stretches

8
00:00:53,487 --> 00:01:00,515
The emerald line is our Safest Route

9
00:01:00,515 --> 00:01:07,543
SafeWalk introduces Explainable Segment-Level Route Intelligence, dividing the walking path into 100 to 200 meter sections

10
00:01:07,543 --> 00:01:14,572
For each segment, our engine reveals exact evidence: commercial footfall, street lighting, and diurnal time penalties

11
00:01:14,572 --> 00:01:21,600
Most importantly, we distinguish safety from data confidence so unmonitored roads are never falsely marked safe

12
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:30,635
When a user feels uncomfortable or followed, she opens SafeStops

13
00:01:30,635 --> 00:01:39,670
SafeStops indexes vetted assistance havens: 24/7 police stations, campus security desks, emergency hospitals, and verified late-night pharmacies

14
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:48,705
We enforce strict data provenance, distinguishing open public facilities from partner-verified institutional desks

15
00:01:48,705 --> 00:01:57,740
With one tap on Navigate to Nearest Help Point, SafeWalk calculates the safest walking path directly to the closest safe haven with instant contact options

16
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:04,892
For lone journeys, users activate Live Journey Guardian: a privacy-first tracking and automated check-in engine

17
00:02:04,892 --> 00:02:12,044
Users set a check-in interval with a grace period

18
00:02:12,044 --> 00:02:19,196
SafeWalk issues a high-entropy 32-byte cryptographic sharing token, never exposing database IDs

19
00:02:19,196 --> 00:02:26,348
During the trip, periodic check-ins confirm user safety

20
00:02:26,348 --> 00:02:33,500
If a check-in is missed or emergency assistance is triggered, our server immediately dispatches simulated alerts to trusted contacts, who can acknowledge that help is on the way

21
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:41,312
SafeWalk also features Multilingual AI Voice Reporting

22
00:02:41,312 --> 00:02:49,125
Users can speak naturally in Hindi, English, or Hinglish

23
00:02:49,125 --> 00:02:56,938
Our NLP engine detects Romanized Hinglish, preserves spoken transcripts, and drafts structured reports for user confirmation

24
00:02:56,938 --> 00:03:04,750
And in low-connectivity areas, SafeWalk works offline as a PWA, queueing incident reports locally with cryptographic idempotency keys that sync automatically once back online

25
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:13,663
For campus administrations and municipal authorities, SafeWalk provides an interactive Safety Intelligence Dashboard

26
00:03:13,663 --> 00:03:22,577
All metrics are computed directly from live database records

27
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:31,490
Authorities can monitor infrastructure gaps like streetlight outages and examine privacy-preserving geospatial risk clusters to plan preventive safety audits without compromising individual travel histories

28
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:41,667
Under the hood, SafeWalk is built on Python, Streamlit, Folium, and SQLite, powered by OSRM pedestrian routing, OpenStreetMap Overpass spatial queries, and Google Gemini AI grounded in safety standards

29
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:51,843
With over 35 structured commits and comprehensive tests, SafeWalk RaahSaathi ensures women don't just reach their destination faster, but safer

30
00:03:51,843 --> 00:04:02,020
Once again, I am Prince Pundir, and thank you for watching
